  "operation": "harvest",
  "summary": "Dev canonical skill 2.19.0 -> 2.20.0: split the single fixed-approval pattern into two named companions per developer request. patterns/approvals.md renamed to patterns/approval-sign-off.md (unconditional gates only, unchanged behavior) plus a cross-reference note. New patterns/approval-intelligent.md defines a distinct, narrower mechanism for checkpoints where whether human review is warranted depends on the actual generated content: state the materiality criterion first, escalate to a full sign-off on any doubt, or auto-approve with a mandatory logged rationale in the artifact the developer already reads -- never a silent skip. Explicitly scoped to never touch a gate already on approval-sign-off.md's fixed list. Wired into three designated checkpoints: Plan Step 4's architecture-audit rework diff (mechanical single-purpose fixes auto-approve; anything changing scope/approach still signs off, and Step 5's whole-plan sign-off still reviews the result either way), Ceremony Step 1's tracker assign/transition (auto-approves when the ticket is unassigned or already the current user's and in a pre-work status; escalates if already assigned elsewhere, past In Progress, or the next status isn't obvious -- reads the ticket's actual state first, never assumes), and Document Step 5's decisions/tech-debt review (auto-approves when every finding/TD row/tracker task is already resolved with no risk-acceptance or deferral implied, formalizing what was previously an informal skip).",
  "package_version": "7.24.0",
